{"answerText":"NYC Planning’s **supplied snapshot metadata** for ZR § 42-00 identifies the section as added effective **December 15, 1961** (CP15820), then amended effective **August 15, 1974** (CP22683); **September 19, 1985** (N850720ZRY); **October 25, 1993** (N930327CZRY); **October 25, 1995** (N950384ZRY); **September 9, 2004** (N040202ZRY); **February 2, 2011** (N110090AZRY); **October 10, 2013** (N130331AZRY); **December 6, 2023** (N230113ZRY); and **December 5, 2024** (N240290ZRY). The metadata identifies amendment events and CPC report links, with short descriptions including the 2023 removal of specified Use Groups and the 2024 removal of an inapplicable section and cross-reference updates. (ZR § 42-00 amendment-history metadata.)

That metadata is an amendment-event index, not historical enacted text: it accompanies the section text but does not reproduce every historical version of § 42-00. The supplied enacted § 42-00 describes the Manufacturing District use-group framework and states that its use provisions may be modified or superseded by special rules in Articles I and VI and Special Purpose Districts. That supplied passage does not establish the wording in force on an earlier date. (ZR § 42-00.)

Accordingly, before reconstructing § 42-00 for a particular date, a professional must verify the historical enacted text in force on that date rather than rely on the metadata alone. The supplied materials do not identify a particular target date or establish which historical version controlled a specific matter.","supportedPointUpserts":[{"targetIndex":0,"value":{"heading":"Supplied amendment-history events for Section 42-00","explanation":"The official NYC Planning amendment-history metadata supplied in this record identifies Section 42-00 as added effective December 15, 1961 (CP15820), and as amended effective August 15, 1974 (CP22683); September 19, 1985 (N850720ZRY); October 25, 1993 (N930327CZRY); October 25, 1995 (N950384ZRY); September 9, 2004 (N040202ZRY); February 2, 2011 (N110090AZRY); October 10, 2013 (N130331AZRY); December 6, 2023 (N230113ZRY); and December 5, 2024 (N240290ZRY). It identifies amendment events and report links, but does not reproduce every historical version of the section.","sectionID":"20017271","sourceIDs":["research-metadata-zoning-amendment-history-a0c7210b20faf0f53be44e8b"]}},{"targetIndex":1,"value":{"heading":"Supplied Section 42-00 passage does not reconstruct prior text","explanation":"The supplied enacted text of Section 42-00 sets out the Manufacturing District use-group structure and states that its use provisions may be modified or superseded by special rules in Articles I and VI and Special Purpose Districts. This supplied passage does not establish the text in force on an earlier date.","sectionID":"20017271","sourceIDs":["9f00cb3d-e984-4cdc-a352-85b31a5ee31e"]}}],"supportedPointRemovals":[],"citationUpserts":[{"targetIndex":1,"value":{"sectionID":"20017271","sourceIDs":["9f00cb3d-e984-4cdc-a352-85b31a5ee31e"],"relevance":"Supplied enacted text of Section 42-00 describing the Manufacturing District use-group framework and stating that use provisions may be modified or superseded by specified special rules; it does not establish historical wording for an earlier date."}}],"citationRemovals":[],"missingFactsAdd":[],"missingFactsRemove":[],"evidenceLimitationsAdd":[],"evidenceLimitationsRemove":[],"additionalEvidenceNeededAdd":[],"additionalEvidenceNeededRemove":["For a date-specific reconstruction: the enrolled/adopted text for each amendment bracketing the target date, the preceding version of Section 42-00, and any applicable effective-date or transition text. If a project is involved, the relevant permit/application and approval record may also be needed to assess any date-based transition route."]}

{"answerText":"**No maximum permitted residential FAR can be selected from the supplied facts.** The proposed building’s ratio is **4.0 FAR** (40,000 sq ft ÷ 10,000 sq ft), but that calculation does not establish that 4.0 FAR is permitted.

The Zoning Resolution makes the zoning maps—including amendments—part of the Resolution, and those maps establish district locations and boundaries (ZR § 11-14). Because the controlling mapped zoning district for this Bronx site has not been established, the applicable residential FAR rule and any district- or special-district conditions cannot be identified from the supplied evidence.

An address or BBL plus the controlling official zoning-map or verified mapped-district evidence is needed before a permitted residential FAR can be determined. The stated 4.0 FAR is only the proposal’s ratio, not an entitlement or compliance conclusion.","supportedPoints":[{"heading":"Zoning-map status controls district applicability","explanation":"ZR § 11-14 provides that the locations and boundaries of districts established by the Resolution are shown on the zoning maps, which are incorporated into the Resolution in their entirety, including amendments. Without the site’s controlling mapped district, the supplied evidence does not establish a residential FAR limit for this site.","sectionID":"20018425","sourceIDs":["33dbba2c-849e-498c-952b-8bfae11e28dc"]}],"assumptions":[],"missingFacts":["The site’s controlling official mapped zoning district, established through a usable property identifier (such as address or BBL) and the controlling official zoning map or verified mapped-district evidence."],"followUpQuestions":["What is the site address or BBL, and what controlling official zoning-map or verified mapped-district evidence identifies its district?"],"evidenceLimitations":["The supplied enacted evidence establishes that zoning maps control district locations and boundaries, but it does not supply the site’s mapped district or a residential FAR provision for that district. This answer uses the NYC Zoning Resolution text through 2026-08-13, which is continuously amended."],"additionalEvidenceNeeded":["The controlling official zoning-map or verified mapped-district evidence for the identified site.","The enacted residential FAR provision applicable to the established mapped district and any established special-district or other mapped overlay condition."],"supportingSourceUses":[],"citations":[{"sectionID":"20018425","sourceIDs":["33dbba2c-849e-498c-952b-8bfae11e28dc"],"relevance":"ZR § 11-14 incorporates zoning maps into the Resolution and establishes that district locations and boundaries are shown on those maps."}]}
